T*
(Statement: An engineering design team is sizing the electric powertrain for an electric) Tj
T*
(passenger vehicle with the following vehicle dynamics parameters:) Tj
T*
(- Curb mass including passengers: M = 1,600 kg) Tj
T*
(- Frontal area: A = 2.2 m^2) Tj
T*
(- Aerodynamic drag coefficient: C_d = 0.28) Tj
T*
(- Air density at 25 deg C: rho = 1.20 kg/m^3) Tj
T*
(- Coefficient of rolling resistance: C_rr = 0.012) Tj
T*
(- Acceleration due to gravity: g = 9.81 m/s^2) Tj
T*
(\(a\) Calculate the steady-state mechanical power \(kW\) required at the wheels to cruise at) Tj
T*
(a highway speed of v = 108 km/h \(30 m/s\) on a flat road.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) Calculate the peak acceleration power \(kW\) required to accelerate from 0 to 100 km/h) Tj
T*
(\(0 to 27.78 m/s\) in t_acc = 7.5 seconds on level ground \(assuming average speed = 13.89) Tj
T*
(m/s\).) Tj
T*
(\(c\) Determine the minimum usable battery pack capacity \(kWh\) to achieve a driving range) Tj
T*
(of 350 km at 108 km/h, assuming powertrain efficiency eta_drive = 88% and Depth of) Tj
T*
(Discharge DoD = 85%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Solution:) Tj
T*
(1. Calculation of Highway Cruising Power \(at v = 30 m/s\):) Tj
T*
(- Rolling resistance force: F_rr = C_rr * M * g = 0.012 * 1,600 * 9.81 = 188.35 N) Tj
T*
