45 780 Td
(harmonic currents as follows:) Tj
T*
(- Fundamental \(50 Hz\): I_1 = 300 A) Tj
T*
(- 5th Harmonic \(250 Hz\): I_5 = 60 A) Tj
T*
(- 7th Harmonic \(350 Hz\): I_7 = 42 A) Tj
T*
(- 11th Harmonic \(550 Hz\): I_11 = 25 A) Tj
T*
(- 13th Harmonic \(650 Hz\): I_13 = 18 A) Tj
T*
(\(a\) Calculate the Total Harmonic Distortion of current \(THD_i\) and the true RMS current) Tj
T*
(drawn from the transformer.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) If IEEE 519 standard mandates THD_i < 8.0%, evaluate if the system violates) Tj
T*
(compliance.) Tj
T*
(\(c\) Design a single-tuned LC passive harmonic filter tuned to the 5th harmonic \(f_tune =) Tj
T*
(250 Hz\) that supplies 75 kVAR of fundamental reactive power to correct the displacement) Tj
T*
(power factor.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Solution:) Tj
T*
(1. Calculation of Total Harmonic Current and True RMS Current:) Tj
T*
(- Harmonic sum of squares: I_harm^2 = I_5^2 + I_7^2 + I_11^2 + I_13^2) Tj
T*
(I_harm^2 = 60^2 + 42^2 + 25^2 + 18^2 = 3600 + 1764 + 625 + 324 = 6,313 A^2) Tj
T*
(I_harm = sqrt\(6,313\) = 79.45 A) Tj
T*
(- Total Harmonic Distortion: THD_i = \(I_harm / I_1\) * 100 = \(79.45 / 300\) * 100 = 26.48%) Tj
T*
(- True RMS Current: I_rms = sqrt\(I_1^2 + I_harm^2\) = sqrt\(300^2 + 79.45^2\) = sqrt\(90,000) Tj
T*
(+ 6,313\) = 310.34 A.) Tj
T*
(- Compliance Evaluation: Measured THD_i = 26.48% severely violates IEEE 519 limit of) Tj
T*
(8.0%. Active or passive filtering is legally required.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Design of Single-Tuned 5th Harmonic Filter Branch:) Tj
T*
(- Tuning order: n = f_tune / f_1 = 250 / 50 = 5.0 \(often tuned to n = 4.8 to avoid) Tj
T*
(anti-resonance tolerances\).) Tj
T*
(- Three-phase filter capacitive reactive power: Q_f = 75 kVAR = 75,000 VAR.) Tj
